      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly difficult to detect covert tracking because the monitoring is designed to be invisible, operating beneath the surface of normal function. If your patterns change, it could be a direct consequence of the data collection itself, creating a feedback loop of anxiety and behavioral alteration. The most robust defense is to be highly skeptical of any device that promises deep, holistic insight into your physical or mental state, and to minimize the personal data you allow them to ingest.",
